#{[17592186393884 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393884 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78552" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393884 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393884 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z=-4 \\\\ -4x+4y-3z=7 \\\\ x-y+z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393884 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07f12953-92a4-55d6-afcb-39fb0f43a712" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393884 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=2,z=-1.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+2+(-1)=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186393887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393885 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b5d59287-5dfe-56f3-93e2-54429b0c04b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393886 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393886 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393886 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3d740f60-2523-5646-9a92-3c0d339e8fc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393887 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393887 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393887 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b7f32d4d-f862-5218-b3d1-078edcdfe213" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393888 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393888 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393888 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "12eac5a8-05a9-5828-8db5-751459d1b149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393889 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393889 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393889 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5af9cd45-f4f1-5692-8de2-840ab3c6c7fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393890 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393890 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393890 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "44860cb9-5129-5c07-80fe-7caff5e9aed0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394270 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394270 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394270 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394270 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0c/0c2f0240b962701c2eb2ee34a0eddc164afb8e1a677a5ed7f81fe65efb890358.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394270 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6c0ad4a3-22f9-57a4-8323-31593f95cf81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394270 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of $\\{i,j\\}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =A(i)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =A(j)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/4e/4e0e5c9cee037bded1f5739af35c3a8acfaa4d4e6f469b3e50afe69b96990e39.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\pi $ radians (counterclockwise or clockwise) about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ (counterclockwise or clockwise) by an angle of $\\pi $ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](images/57/578b3315028bf5a19a4b6e17d228db08b41f24dee63e5cb7f8d601ce667785f4.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186394274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394271 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8eaae499-eee4-5eed-af75-d74268bec6c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394272 #edb/ref 1080 "images/b6/b66fd6bb3e9b37fd3a72927a1fb4df87eaffea3bf5579e681fee3aeda4885e75.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394272 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394272 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dcbf67f7-3f48-58b0-b313-1ddf0a908258" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394273 #edb/ref 1080 "images/aa/aa78e1ab38afbc0cd7bf92061d176a816c7a8a0e1d08c8825486c45dbe8fb5f5.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394273 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394273 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8d294a24-e87b-5b66-a362-f26102dab0e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394274 #edb/ref 1080 "images/39/39168e3de9d42254e0c1528ab7ed40f2a4c0e88e9570705b773e3875d5057df2.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394274 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394274 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b69504f-e290-5883-87fb-ed2e3d29bb3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394275 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c9/c95c1f93ccc6c6c2ff7264ac5bca90680ff2c3c745d95acb0f81d288bf4e498a.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394275 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394275 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bfa84fc9-3d0a-59df-b5c7-bacc5b53fb4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394276 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d6/d64f49a072fd7841d1d1b81e396673f3addcfa05005128e969dbb6ea4697d358.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394276 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394276 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb14ca5e-3e3c-5a83-b18e-eead2e86a390" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394284 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394284 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394284 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f7/f7f75505591eb8bf407e63b4255ae65548bde65921f6f00cca9031191ddc0905.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394284 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7364bd3c-e82a-5e8d-b8cd-06a6c72405af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394284 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of $\\{i,j\\}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =Ai=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =Aj=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/77/77936c4115b37d79ae301a93b218ecd23114ae4ad42d8298b8f058c1f50e82a2.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ **clockwise** by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/ab6a3ec35954243105f9bb6c9f1f2cc21c02358f90855f9f36f0a590092eb93d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186394286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394285 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f5bbd5a5-fd75-5bef-9814-1007ac35605e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394286 #edb/ref 1080 "images/f4/f4d4d52cb24bd1e3dd4bc37736533693ff89e6b08f495f8541f23abde995a5b9.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394286 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394286 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d473b8ea-8d04-5ece-95ea-65e737aef3a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394287 #edb/ref 1080 "images/97/979157d993a86617fabf4b2dfacc6d4c1d973885b42be081b4bcffb36058e091.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394287 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394287 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03ae5c24-7a66-5265-969a-3f12d946ddaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394288 #edb/ref 1080 "images/4b/4bf42e3bdeb61feccd68cf4eeb9e3c4a40e8b903a5739df77c993e9aa4abc993.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394288 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394288 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47c3f52d-cad6-592b-8617-cf6147446ba0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394289 #edb/ref 1080 "images/cf/cf449d44237c85963bf4fbb134da290b39aac4ebd0b128313052cbd1970db67f.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394289 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394289 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d69be06f-7ba5-5d06-aad7-b3459d303317" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394290 #edb/ref 1080 "images/5b/5b4684361e541532d1be24de046f17201811146fbb0413222c5100e5a3eb80dc.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394290 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394290 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2ef8d4dc-0422-509e-9d94-1b349ccfac6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394359 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394359 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394359 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394359 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394359 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df7a9928-b595-5d80-8b20-2abd529873c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394359 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/75/75f9c68145ed74a2c3530012061eb65cd93bae38d82fa0d34e5dc042f8073841.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le x-2\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=x-2\\,⟹\\,x=y+2\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=4.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y-2\\le x\\le 4\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/57/575e7e482f88635f6267405f66857a5488dac79833fce16d3d998df19e24d119.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y+2}^{4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186394363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394360 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "731178a8-5a8e-5ed8-9f30-da952012cffd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394361 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{y+2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394361 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394361 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2deb6544-dffe-5ba9-b24a-d293aa2fbbc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394362 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{y+2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394362 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394362 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "669b98bf-31e0-5013-9ac0-599f9b3ac451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394363 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y+2}^{4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394363 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394363 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23039d9f-352c-59fe-86a0-167d83ce168f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394364 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{y+2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394364 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394364 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "433f56d3-0b58-5e90-bed9-f07ced243d50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394365 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{y+2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394365 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394365 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e2c2997-4b5f-5ed6-8c44-7810dc10c72c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394627 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394627 #edb/ref 1069 "q-85044" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394627 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394627 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $(\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394627 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ccb665c6-b272-5591-95cb-e38be54fe76e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394627 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{20}{16})$ means the same thing as ${}_{20}{C}_{16}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=20$ and $r=16,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{20}{C}_{16} & =\\frac{20!}{(20-16)!16!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20!}{4!16!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\cdot 