633 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394633 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f9dca18c-0cda-53f2-ae56-98a74295c88b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394827 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394827 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394827 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394827 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the diagrams shows the solution of the following system?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x \\\\ y\\le -2x\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394827 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "12b718de-1f28-5ec6-b73e-0c704e48e717" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394827 #edb/ref 1074 "To graph the first inequality $y\\le 2x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=2x.$\n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y\\le -2x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=-2x.$ \n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](images/43/438928da5e9de5e9ba3d2abbe06b6f1f8b6b0598a0b82bec1f51824b9ef72a71.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186394833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394828 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7c907422-6a43-51a3-a689-8ba380b4f66e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394829 #edb/ref 1080 "images/bb/bb0ea125af03527a6e3111fc638f5fd9a4efaa39bc7b48a82e2efcfcfb0b696b.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394829 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394829 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "338a182a-eee2-5984-9c16-ac8f5df92c94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394830 #edb/ref 1080 "images/27/27ba3ad2783e64a6b29d5ea488d63fc634d2a43ee01d6a77c4802da8bc06b641.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394830 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394830 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3faab0ae-2527-51e9-960b-f170f93df96e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394831 #edb/ref 1080 "images/e5/e5428cead5e96d930e52a833942a1c4452c43f3e2f6ba7c6fc39758ee83e8d81.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394831 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394831 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a6ca9e1d-7076-5b73-a120-7f365e92f4c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394832 #edb/ref 1080 "images/19/197ae7933ece17a22bdf17c2397053541891a789892813599930de273496cd78.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394832 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394832 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "55b6c46d-d1d1-5590-9b0c-83f0e901feca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394833 #edb/ref 1080 "images/43/438928da5e9de5e9ba3d2abbe06b6f1f8b6b0598a0b82bec1f51824b9ef72a71.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394833 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394833 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "547435a9-62b0-54fe-88c5-c2df65965648" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105291" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1071 "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "faa7ddb4-5b88-5e56-a53e-35fdb9d2ef93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/r