" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396708 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1040f4bd-3d1a-5f7b-8b2b-4c581d4ad345" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396708 #edb/ref 1074 "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of $\\{i,j\\}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/b9/b93bb91dae85a3e3b40a8d0ade3d4f420064aaa6926431fa7f664c977bb8fd59.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396713 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396709 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d53d07f6-e520-5ab9-8077-eda6c3ac37ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396710 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396710 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396710 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c162ec8c-668b-5bfc-ab